unrestrictedWarnDetail:
An application you select will be able to:
• use every API without declaring it: read the clipboard, reach the network, read and write the files it stored, send notifications;
• reach addresses on this computer and your local network (router, intranet services, local development servers);
• ignore storage quotas, file size limits and rate limits, so it can fill the disk or freeze the page.

It still runs in a sandbox and cannot read your other tabs or system files.

If someone else asked you to turn this on, think it over very carefully.
